aibox brings up a reference LLM inference platform on Kubernetes (locally on kind
or on AWS EKS), runs reproducible benchmarks and reports cost per 1M tokens and latency.

Usage:
  aibox [command]

Available Commands:
  bench       Run a declared benchmark experiment
  cost        Show the accumulated cost of the current cloud run
  doctor      Check prerequisites for a profile (tools, container runtime, AWS quotas)
  down        Tear down the platform for a profile and check for orphans
  help        Help about any command
  models      List and mirror catalog models
  render      Render generated platform manifests from a profile
  report      Generate the benchmark report from results
  smoke       Send one request per model and check metrics, traces and dashboards
  ttl         Show or extend the automatic teardown time of the current cloud run
  up          Bring up the platform for a profile (cluster, GitOps, workloads)
  version     Print version information

Flags:
      --dry-run          print external commands instead of running them
  -h, --help             help for aibox
  -o, --output string    output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string   profile name (profiles/<name>.yaml) or path to a profile file (default "local")
  -v, --verbose          verbose (debug) logging on stderr
  -y, --yes              assume yes for confirmations

Use "aibox [command] --help" for more information about a command.
